  "markdown": "\n## 2026-11-25 end-of-day reflection (close run 16:41 ET)\n\nFacts from paper ledgers (fills.csv, trades.csv, nav.csv, sleeve_equity.csv, positions.csv, dx_log, watchlist_decisions, bar_checks, movers_log, alerts, shadow_summary/shadow_check output). No Claude/Sonnet call was used; the factual reflection was written directly from the files (usage economy, no replacement batch). Every figure below is from those files or arithmetic on them.\n\n**Headline:** Account is trailing SPY. Time-weighted return -7.82% vs SPY-equivalent -6.16% (-1.66 pts); equity $19,699.77 vs $19,655.43 SPY-eq on $19,852.34 net contributions. Day (no deposits): NAV 19,773.99 -> 19,699.77 = -0.375% vs SPY-eq 19,712.48 -> 19,655.43 = -0.289%, so the account lagged SPY by ~0.09 pts on the day and the cumulative gap widened from -1.585 to -1.659 pts. Sleeves vs SPY-eq: Signals -7.16% vs -6.16% (day -0.48% vs -0.29%); Day-trade -4.92% vs -5.72% (+0.80 pts, mostly idle SPY, not a DX result); Momentum -28.74% (-22.6 pts vs SPY; day -1.57%); Earnings -7.93%; Core/Dividend equal SPY.\n\n**Paper trades today (only close trades; no entries or exits at the open or intraday):**\n- Day-trade: SELL TGT 2.367783 @172.1339 (16:00 daily close 172.22, DX TIME STOP 5 trading days; one_filter waived two_source), +$7.58 / +1.894% from 168.9344. This exit used the daily close, not a 5-min bar. BUY SPY 0.568400 @717.0584 ($407.58 idle cash).\n- Signals, Momentum, Core, Dividend, Earnings: no trades. Earnings sleeve had no exits (DE exited 11-24 before the report).\n- No DX entries, no Signals orders, no skips other than SNY (gap-up >3%: 3.97% premarket, rechecked 3.31% at 08:46 ET, stayed skipped by rule).\n\n**Day-trade experiment (DX), 7 closed:** two_source n=5 (win 60%, avg +1.249%, +$18.46); ma50 n=1 (-4.074%, -$16.30); gap_up_3pct n=1 (-3.021%, -$7.55). Closed total -$5.39, 3 wins / 7 (43%), average return about -0.12% (arithmetic on the status table). Open at close (stock only, marks from positions.csv): RGA +$10.29 (+2.57%), EXPD +$2.93 (+1.17%), DG +$11.52 (+4.61%). No setup near 20 closed trades; the 2026-12-18 review is pending. Entry distance: n<10 closed-with-distance is 7, not evaluated; no new DX fill today, so nothing new vs prior close/open/VWAP. Invalidation alerts: RGA (265.55) and EXPD (193.12) were breached 11-20; neither stopped out and both are green now; DG's 130.53 not breached (low 137.19). Alerts have not yet preceded a stop (A and PDD are the stopped DX names; n too small). No DX entry relied on a default warning level today (no entries). TGT: +1.89% over 5 trading days while SPY (sold at 731.594 on 11-18 to fund it, 716.70 now) fell ~2.0%; TGT is a low-beta name (0.4) in a down tape and n=1: beta/regime, not skill.\n\n**Watch list (v0.5.15):** 6 names, 0 undecided: 0 entered, 0 rejected, 1 no-setup (WDAY), 4 cancelled (NTNX, AMBA, URBN, DE), 1 blocked (DELL, cross-sleeve >10% loss rule). All decided same day; none retrospective.\n\n**Bar checks:** 88 rows today, all result 'none' (no stops/targets hit), 0 quote fallbacks. Movers scan flagged names (SNDK -28%, MU, BE, LITE, WDC, AMD, MRVL, STX, TER, INTC, NVDA, AMBA, NTNX, TSLA, P, J, MRNA at ~11:32 ET; AI/semis selloff). Movers is awareness only; held names were handled by existing stops (none hit). I did not pull closing moves for those names, so I make no claim about their closes.\n\n**Mistakes / misses (actual):**\n- Momentum semis/storage book remains the largest drag: -28.74%, -22.6 pts vs SPY. I have not proposed a rule since Nov 6; this is a repeat of 'flagged risk not escalated' (tally +1). The sleeve is $107, so account P&L effect is small, but the pattern is the same.\n- Cancelled bounces: DE cancelled at 07:52 ET (guide below consensus, PM only -2.4%, not a >=5% gap); at 10:34 ET DE was +2.75% vs prior close and +7.25% vs the open. AMBA (cancelled) was -19.97% vs prior close but +5.75% vs the open at 11:32. NTNX (cancelled) was -4.09% vs open at 11:32, so that cancel avoided a further drop. These were rule-correct decisions; I cannot say DE or AMBA would have been tradable at those prices, so no profit claim. Net of the three: one loss avoided (NTNX), two names that rose from the open after cancel.\n- WDAY: PM -9.6%, but it opened -2.3% below prior close (never reached the <=170.27 trigger at 09:45+; low 173.00) and recovered to +2.0% by 10:34. no-setup, correct under the rule.\n- SNY upgrade skipped by the gap-up >3% rule (3.31% at the recheck). Not a rule slip; PM shadow tracked SNY +0.35% over 1 day. No claim.\n- Data gap: shadow intraday spread snapshot at 16:42 ET had 0/94 usable quotes (market POST), so measured spreads are not available from this run; modeled costs only.\n\n**Overeager / too cautious:** No overeager trades (no entries). No source-count issue today. Cancelling all 4 negative-news bounces is within the written 'clearly negative news not waivable' text; n too small to say it was too cautious.\n\n**Shadows (no paper money):** F50: SMTC closed -12.202% (excess -10.53% vs SPY); SHLS entered 11-25 @6.395, now +10.62% net (open, +8.70% excess, one day). F50x single-source still fails (49 closed, 10.2% win, -6.03%/trade evidence only); F50_below50d_only 8 closed, 25% win, -1.343%, under 30, not judged. Test B (RSI2): PFE closed +3.970% net; PM pending exit; MPC/VLO/PSX bought 11-25 (three correlated energy refiners; one theme, not three samples); 28 closed, win 60.7%, -0.106%/trade, not meeting the bar. Test Z (REJECT backtest): 14 closed, win 21.4%, -3.735%/trade; ACN/MRK/JPM/PFE still holding. A gap-and-go: 13 trades, -0.008%/trade, under 30. squeeze_bb30: 0 trades. IL intraday lab: today's forward avg +1.012% across 312 shadow longs on a selloff day; cumulative IL setups remain negative (e.g. IL_orb5 1128 trades -0.496%), a one-day average is not evidence. PM shadow: SNY +0.35% closed; PM_open baselines still negative. No pass claims; failed variants preserved.\n\n**What worked:** TGT DX time stop banked +$7.58 (beta/regime, n=1). Cancels and blocks (DELL cross-sleeve) avoided entering falling names (NTNX clearly; DELL not priced here). Staying in DX cash/SPY on a selloff day protected nothing meaningful beyond beta; Day-trade -0.27% vs account -0.375% is mostly idle SPY.\n**Lesson:** Cancelled-bounce outcomes are mixed on day one (NTNX fell further, DE/AMBA rose from the open); collect outcomes per decision before judging the 'negative news not waivable' text. No new rule suggested, no rule changed today.\n"
